# Step 4: Income account, independently estimated

Now we do it **without** taking ₹4,772 and slicing it like a birthday cake.

## Formula

[
GDP_{movie}^{(Y)} = W + OS + MI + (T-S)
]

I’ll estimate each block from the franchise structure, not from the final expenditure result.

---

## 4A. Compensation of employees (W)

This includes:

* cast
* crew
* post-production staff
* marketing labour
* exhibition staff attributable to the run
* related local service labour

### Production-side labour

Assume labour share of all-in franchise cost:

[
W_{production} = 42% \times 505 = 212.10
]

### Exhibition + concession + local service labour

This should be estimated from the downstream consumer activity, not from budget.

Assume labour share on:

* concessions
* adjacent spend
* exhibitor-side theatre operations attributable to the run

Use:

* 14% of ticket gross as exhibitor/service labour attributable to the film
* 18% of concessions
* 22% of adjacent spend

So:

[
W_{tickets,service} = 0.14 \times 2722.19 = 381.11
]

[
W_{conc} = 0.18 \times 734.99 = 132.30
]

[
W_{adj} = 0.22 \times 108.89 = 23.96
]

Thus total labour compensation:

[
W = 212.10 + 381.11 + 132.30 + 23.96
]

[
W = 749.47
]

---

## 4B. Taxes less subsidies ((T-S))

This should also be estimated independently.

### Ticket-side net product tax

Use effective tax rate on tickets:

[
\tau_{tickets} = 12%
]

[
T_{tickets} = 0.12 \times 2722.19 = 326.66
]

### Concession taxes

[
\tau_{conc} = 18%
]

[
T_{conc} = 0.18 \times 734.99 = 132.30
]

### Other fees / permits

Assume:

[
T_{other} = 6.00
]

### Less subsidy

[
S = G = 7.58
]

So:

[
(T-S) = 326.66 + 132.30 + 6.00 - 7.58 = 457.38
]

---

## 4C. Mixed income / rents / finance (MI)

This includes:

* equipment rentals
* location rents
* financing margin
* royalty-linked smaller rights flows
* lending / leasing income

Estimate from cost structure and rights flows.

### Rent + finance on cost side

[
MI_{costside} = 12% \times 505 = 60.60
]

### Rights-linked mixed income

Assume 25% of total rights package accrues as royalty / finance / licensing income rather than corporate surplus:

[
MI_{rights} = 0.25 \times 380 = 95.00
]

So:

[
MI = 60.60 + 95.00 = 155.60
]

---

## 4D. Operating surplus (OS)

Now estimate from actual channels, independently.

### Producer/distributor surplus

Start with franchise cash-in side:

* India net = 2300.25
* assume producer/distributor share of India net:

[
r_{pd,India} = 50.5%
]

[
PD_{India} = 0.505 \times 2300.25 = 1161.63
]

* overseas realization rate:

[
r_{pd,Overseas} = 42%
]

[
PD_{Overseas} = 0.42 \times 660.31 = 277.33
]

* rights inflow:
  [
  PD_{Rights} = 380.00
  ]

So total producer/distributor inflow:

[
PD_{gross} = 1161.63 + 277.33 + 380.00 = 1818.96
]

Now strip out production labour and cost-side mixed income already counted:

[
OS_{prod/dist} = 1818.96 - 212.10 - 60.60 = 1546.26
]

### Exhibitor/local-service surplus

This should come from ticket-side exhibitor share plus concession and adjacent margin.

India-side exhibitor share:

[
r_{exh} = 49.5%
]

[
ExhibitorShare = 0.495 \times 2300.25 = 1138.62
]

Now remove labour already counted on that side:

[
OS_{exhibition/local} =
1138.62 + 734.99 + 108.89 - 381.11 - 132.30 - 23.96
]

[
OS_{exhibition/local} = 1445.13
]

So total operating surplus:

[
OS = 1546.26 + 1445.13 = 2991.39
]

---

## 4E. Final income result

[
GDP_{movie}^{(Y)} = W + OS + MI + (T-S)
]

[
GDP_{movie}^{(Y)} = 749.47 + 2991.39 + 155.60 + 457.38
]

[
GDP_{movie}^{(Y)} = 4353.84
]

## Income headline

[
\boxed{GDP_{movie}^{(Y)} = ₹4,353.84 \text{ crore}}
]

That is **independently estimated**.

And notice what happened: it does **not** exactly match expenditure. Good. That is actually more believable.

